        {
            "timestamp": 1589578996,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Matt Spinler",
                "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                "username": "spinler"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\nI tried this out, and for the processors, because they're on DCMs (which when I first wrote this I knew there was a hole) it still just repeats cpus 0 & 1 again with no hint they're on DCMs.  Ideas on what can be done there?  Call them procs 0,1,2,3 instead?"
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1590686258,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Santosh Puranik",
                "email": "santosh.puranik.ibm@gmail.com",
                "username": "santoshpuranik"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2: Code-Review-1\n\n> Patch Set 2:\n> \n> I tried this out, and for the processors, because they're on DCMs (which when I first wrote this I knew there was a hole) it still just repeats cpus 0 & 1 again with no hint they're on DCMs.  Ideas on what can be done there?  Call them procs 0,1,2,3 instead?\n\nI think calling them cpu0 through cpu3 will work. We can then abstract away the FRU VPD EEPROM vs module VPD EEPROM within the VPD manager."
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1590686363,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Santosh Puranik",
                "email": "santosh.puranik.ibm@gmail.com",
                "username": "santoshpuranik"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\nPriyanga, this looks good overall, we just need a way to handle the CPU modules. Instead of repeating cpu0 and cpu1 twice over like this does now, could you change it instead to go by the chip target for CPUs and emit cpu0, cpu1, cpu2, cpu3 .... and so on? That should cover the DCM cases."
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1590769186,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Matt Spinler",
                "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                "username": "spinler"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\nAlso, there FRU_PATH attributes call out the BMC card a lot with the BMC card target, which is this in the inventory:\n\n   Target:  /sys-0/node-0/nisqually-0/ebmc-card-connector-0/ingraham-0\n   Name:    /system/chassis/motherboard/ebmc_card_ingraham\n\nBut, in inventory manager, it is:\n   /system/chassis/motherboard/ebmc_card_bmc\n\nIdeas on how to get these to agree?"
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1590774861,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Santosh Puranik",
                "email": "santosh.puranik.ibm@gmail.com",
                "username": "santoshpuranik"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n> Patch Set 2:\n> \n> Also, there FRU_PATH attributes call out the BMC card a lot with the BMC card target, which is this in the inventory:\n> \n>    Target:  /sys-0/node-0/nisqually-0/ebmc-card-connector-0/ingraham-0\n>    Name:    /system/chassis/motherboard/ebmc_card_ingraham\n> \n> But, in inventory manager, it is:\n>    /system/chassis/motherboard/ebmc_card_bmc\n> \n> Ideas on how to get these to agree?\nWe'll have to change the one in the inventory to /system/chassis/motherboard/ebmc_card_ingraham, I think. Which was sort of the point of making these updates anyway"
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1590778846,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Matt Spinler",
                "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                "username": "spinler"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n> Patch Set 2:\n> \n> > Patch Set 2:\n> > \n> > Also, there FRU_PATH attributes call out the BMC card a lot with the BMC card target, which is this in the inventory:\n> > \n> >    Target:  /sys-0/node-0/nisqually-0/ebmc-card-connector-0/ingraham-0\n> >    Name:    /system/chassis/motherboard/ebmc_card_ingraham\n> > \n> > But, in inventory manager, it is:\n> >    /system/chassis/motherboard/ebmc_card_bmc\n> > \n> > Ideas on how to get these to agree?\n> We'll have to change the one in the inventory to /system/chassis/motherboard/ebmc_card_ingraham, I think. Which was sort of the point of making these updates anyway\n\nFrom a purely naming perspective, it would be better to not have ingraham in the name I think, but not sure how to accomplish that in the MRW so yea maybe change the inventory."
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1590784324,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "Matt Spinler",
                "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                "username": "spinler"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\nFor the sake of completeness, also the MRW has the following for power supplies:\n\npower_distribution_power_supply_power_supply0  \n\nvs powersupply0 on the BMC"
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1592920048,
            "reviewer": {
